  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 364,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 54353,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 30,
        "headingId": 164,
        "headingText": "<p >The upper, lower, and middle portions of the stomach are affected in decreasing order of frequency {14254074; 26464735}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-04T15:33:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 365,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 54354,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 30,
        "headingId": 165,
        "headingText": "<p >The clinical features are the same as those of other gastric cancers.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-04T15:34:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 366,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 54355,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 30,
        "headingId": 166,
        "headingText": "<p >Limited data are available. Primary gastric squamous cell carcinoma accounts for 0.04&ndash;0.07% of all gastric cancers, and &lt;&nbsp;100&nbsp;cases have been reported {26464735; 14254074; 24765539}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-04T15:34:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 367,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 54356,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 30,
        "headingId": 167,
        "headingText": "<p>Unknown</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-04T15:35:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 368,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 54357,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 30,
        "headingId": 168,
        "headingText": "<p >Various origins have been proposed, including via squamous cell metaplasia of gastric mucosa, from pluripotent stem cells, from ectopic squamous nests in the gastric mucosa, or from gastric carcinoma undergoing squamous metaplasia {24765539; 21113875; 25925374}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-04T15:35:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 375,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 207,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 54358,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 30,
        "headingId": 207,
        "headingText": "<p>The macroscopic appearance is the same as that of other gastric cancers.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-01-29T16:37:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 369,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 54359,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 30,
        "headingId": 169,
        "headingText": "<p>The histology is similar to that of squamous cell carcinoma of the oesophagus (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/31/6\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Oesophageal squamous papilloma</em>) and other organs. The tumour shows uniform squamous cell differentiation and lack of any adenocarcinoma or other histology on thorough sampling. Sufficient sampling to exclude another component is mandatory, as is exclusion of metastasis from squamous cell carcinoma of another organ. Extension from lower oesophageal squamous cell carcinoma should be ruled out.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-06-04T15:35:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 370,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 170,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 54360,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 30,
        "headingId": 170,
        "headingText": "<p>Not clinically relevant</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-01-29T16:38:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 371,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 171,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 54361,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 30,
        "headingId": 171,
        "headingText": "<p>No conclusive data are available.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-01-29T16:38:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 374,
